cts of Baked by Melissa are cupcakes.  \n   - If dried Thai chilies (DTC) are spicy **or** a bakery, then they are a hotpot **or** are spicy.  \n\n2. **Assume the statement is true**:  \n   - \"DTC are cupcakes and a product of Baked by Melissa.\"  \n   - Since they are cupcakes (via Baked by Melissa), they are bakeries (per premise 2).  \n   - As bakeries, they cannot be spicy (per premise 1).  \n\n3. **Apply the fifth premise**:  \n   - **Antecedent**: DTC are a bakery (from above), so the condition \"spicy **or** bakery\" is **true**.  \n   - **Consequent**: Therefore, DTC must be a hotpot **or** spicy.  \n   - Since they are **not spicy** (from step 2), they must be **hotpots** (per the consequent).  \n\n4. **Contradiction**:  \n   - If DTC are hotpots, premise 3 states hotpots are spicy, making DTC spicy.  \n   - This directly contradicts premise 1 (no bakery is spicy), as DTC are a bakery (cupcakes).  \n\nThus, assuming the statement is true leads to a logical contradiction. The statement **cannot be true**.  \n\n**Answer**: **B) False**",
