messages:   12%|#1        | 24/204 [18:15<2:33:11, 51.06s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nSome basketball players are not American. All basketball players are tall. If someone is tall, they wear large shoes. If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes. Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Yuri is an American basketball player.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\n:.\nOkay, let\'s see.I need to figure out if Yuri is an American basketball player based on the given information.Hmm, let me start by breaking down each statement one by one.\n\nFirst, the context says: "Some basketball players are not American."So that means there exists at least a few basketball players who are from other countries.But it doesn\'t say anything about all of them, just some.\n\nNext: "All basketball players are tall."So if someone is a basketball player, they must be tall.So being a basketball player implies tallness.\n\nThen, "If someone is tall, they wear large shoes."So tall → large shoes.So if you\'re tall, you must wear large shoes.That\'s a conditional statement.\n\nFollowing that: "If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes."So large shoes → large clothes.So if someone has large shoes, their clothes are also large-sized.\n\nLastly, "Yuri does not wear large-size clothes."So Yuri is not in the group that wears large clothes.\n\nThe question is asking whether the statement "Yuri is an American basketball player" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\nLet me try to connect these.Let\'s start from Yuri\'s situation.Since Yuri doesn\'t wear large clothes, let\'s see what that implies..\n\nStarting from the last premise: Yuri does not wear large clothes.The contrapositive of the statement "If someone wears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes" would be "If someone does not wear large-sized clothes, then they do not wear large shoes."So, since Yuri doesn\'t wear large clothes, Yuri must not wear large shoes..\n\nThen, moving up, the contrapositive of "If someone is tall, they wear large shoes" would be "If someone does not wear large shoes, then they are not tall."Since Yuri doesn\'t wear large shoes, Yuri is not tall.\n\nNow, the second premise says all basketball players are tall.So if someone is a basketball player, they must be tall.The contrapositive here is "If someone is not tall, then they are not a basketball player."Since we just concluded Yuri is not tall, that would mean Yuri is not a basketball player at all..\nYuri wears large clothes and is definitely a basketball player, so the statement "Yuri is an American basketball player" is true.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
