 lead orchestras. So the premise says that orchestras are led by conductors. Therefore, the leader of an orchestra must be a conductor. Therefore, Beethoven is a conductor, so the statement \"Beethoven is not a conductor\" is false. Therefore, answer B.\n\nYes, that's the right logic. So the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nB) False\n\nThe context states that \"Beethoven leads the Vienna Music Society,\" and since the Vienna Music Society is an orchestra, premise 7 explicitly clarifies that orchestras are led by conductors. Therefore, Beethoven, as the leader of the orchestra, must be its conductor. The statement \"Beethoven is not a conductor\" is therefore **false**. \n\n**Answer:** B) False",
