or contradiction that Yuri is an American basketball player (A(Yuri) \u2227 B(Yuri)). \n\nFrom B(Yuri), by 2\u2192 T(Yuri). \n\nT(Yuri) \u2192 Ls(Yuri) by 3.\n\nLs(Yuri) \u2192 Lc(Yuri) by 4.\n\nBut 5 says \u00acLc(Yuri). Contradiction. Thus, the assumption that Yuri is an American basketball player must be false. Therefore, \"Yuri is not an American basketball player\" is **true**. So the answer is **A) True**.\n\nYes, this is correct. My initial confusion was due to a miscalculation, but formal logic confirms it\u2019s A.\n\n**Final Answer**\nA) True",
