Harry were evil, he would be ugly. But since he is not ugly, Harry cannot be evil.  \n\nFrom the first premise: **A man is either kind or evil**. Since Harry is not evil, he must be **kind**.  \n\nThe statement \"Harry is kind **or** a CEO\" is true because the first condition (\"kind\") is satisfied. Even if Harry is not a CEO, the inclusive \"or\" means the entire statement holds.  \n\n**Answer: A) True**",
