messages:   75%|#######5  | 153/204 [1:28:15<25:19, 29.80s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nBeijing is the capital of the People's Republic of China. Beijing is the world's most populous national capital city. Beijing is located in Northern China. Beijing hosted the 2008 Summer Olympics and 2008 Summer Paralympics Games. Beijing has hosted both the Summer and Winter Olympics, along with the Summer and Winter Paralympics Many of Beijing's 91 universities consistently rank among the best in the Asia-Pacific and the world.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Beijing is located in southern China.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain", '<think>\n:.\nOkay, let me try to figure this out.The question is asking whether the statement "Beijing is located in southern China" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context.The options are A, B, or C.\n\nFirst, I\'ll look at the context provided.The first sentence says, "Beijing is the capital of the People\'s Republic of China."That\'s just stating the obvious.Then the next relevant part is: "Beijing is located in Northern China."Wait, there it is.The context explicitly mentions that Beijing is in Northern China..\n\nThe question\'s statement claims it\'s in southern China.So if the context says Northern, then the statement should be false.The options are A) True, B) False, C) Uncertain..\nWith confidence in the location directly specified, uncertainty is irrelevant. Therefore, the correct answer should be A) True... Therefore, my final option is: ']]
